codex
Implemented and locally verified a Track B generator based on the complete root-of-unity orbit in Theorem 3.2 of the [full paper](https://arxiv.org/html/1101.2994v2#S3.SS1).

Files:

- [gen_1101_2994.py](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1101.2994/gen_1101_2994.py)
- [selftest_report.json](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1101.2994/selftest_report.json)
- [README.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1101.2994/README.md)
- [bare transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1101.2994/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [hinted transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1101.2994/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [placebo transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1101.2994/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

Local gates G1–G8 pass. G9’s size caps also pass: 889 characters, 254 atoms, and 254 intended operations.

The result is not shippable yet: all 12 oracle attempts—four per arm—were rejected with OpenRouter HTTP 403 `Key limit exceeded` before any model responded. Consequently, G9 remains false and `all_passed` is false. The transcripts preserve those harness-generated diagnostics; no hardness evidence was fabricated, and no `REJECTED.md` was created because this is an infrastructure blocker rather than a family failure.
